{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a2052"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c171): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c171.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a2052"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge technology/computing","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/technology__computing.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",778],["+","The prefixes turn up in two more places in every quiz. A digital camera's resolution is quoted in megapixels, and since mega means a million, one megapixel is 1,000,000 pixels: a 12-megapixel phone sensor records twelve million picture points in every shot. At the other end of the scale, supercomputers are rated in FLOPS, floating-point operations per second, so a petaFLOPS is a unit of computer processing speed: 10^15, a thousand trillion calculations every second. IBM's Roadrunner at Los Alamos became the first machine to sustain one petaFLOPS in 2008; the fastest systems of the 2020s have climbed one rung higher, to exaFLOPS.\n\n"],["=",349]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",698],["+","Zwei weitere Stellen kommen in jedem Quiz vor. Die Auflösung einer Digitalkamera wird in Megapixeln angegeben, und da Mega eine Million bedeutet, hat ein Megapixel 1.000.000 Pixel: Ein 12-Megapixel-Sensor im Handy nimmt bei jeder Aufnahme zwölf Millionen Bildpunkte auf. Am anderen Ende der Skala werden Supercomputer in FLOPS gemessen, Gleitkommaoperationen pro Sekunde; ein PetaFLOPS ist also eine Maßeinheit für die Rechengeschwindigkeit von Computern: 10^15, eine Billiarde Rechenschritte in jeder Sekunde. IBMs Roadrunner in Los Alamos hielt 2008 als erster Rechner dauerhaft ein PetaFLOPS durch; die schnellsten Systeme der 2020er-Jahre sind eine Stufe höher bei ExaFLOPS angekommen.\n\n"],["=",339]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a2052"},"reason":"a2052 body: byte/hertz/second ladder sentences rewritten so each answer sits in a sentence stating its order (\"After the terabyte comes the petabyte\" etc.); notes: 1,024 TB is strictly a pebibyte, petabyte expected — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metric_prefix","by":"enrich batch 222","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1908-a2621.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metric_prefix"}]},
